---
/*
  Tussenstand — "Tussenstand: twee antwoorden op één machine" in two columns
  (#131). Wraps the two paragraphs under that heading, not the heading itself
  (that stays a deco h2 of the surrounding Half).

  The first paragraph holds both answers ("Art nouveau antwoordde: … Art deco
  antwoordde: …") and may not be split or reordered, so art-nouveau-en-deco.css
  lets it run on in two columns: the nouveau answer falls on the left, the deco
  answer mostly on the right. The two column heads above it are the only added
  text and only repeat the names of the styles; they are decorative, hence
  aria-hidden. The closing paragraph runs at full width.

  Two columns only when the wrapper is wide enough (a container query in the
  stylesheet), so one column on mobile and on narrow desktop windows, with the
  heads hidden.
*/
---
<div class="tussenstand">
  <div class="tussenstand__heads" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="tussenstand__head tussenstand__head--nouveau">art nouveau</span>
    <span class="tussenstand__head tussenstand__head--deco">art deco</span>
  </div>
  <slot />
</div>
